		<div class="modal fade" id="modal1" >
			<div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable">
			    <div class="modal-content">
			        <div class="modal-header">
			            <h5 class="modal-title" id="exampleModalLabel">Kiaf SEOUL & Frieze Seoul Terms and Conditions</h5>
			            <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
			        </div>
			        <div class="modal-body">
			            <h5 class="text-center">General Terms</h5>
			            <h6>General Terms</h6>
			            <ul class="text-black-50 mb-3 small list-unstyled text-indent-1">
			                <li class="item">
			                    1. GALLERIES ASSOCIATION OF KOREA incorporated and registered at 102-407, 461, Samil-daero, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03147, Korea ("GAoK"); and Frieze Events Ltd incorporated
			                    and registered 1 Surrey Street, London, WC2R 2ND ("Frieze"); each an "Organizer" and together the "Organizers".
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">2. GAoK is the owner, proprietor, organizer and presenter of the Korea International Art Fair "Kiaf SEOUL" held in Seoul, South Korea since 2002.</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    3. Frieze is the owner, proprietor, organizer and presenter of "Frieze Seoul" and Frieze Art Fairs globally, including Frieze London, Frieze Masters, Frieze New York
			                    and Frieze Los Angeles.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">4. Kiaf SEOUL and Frieze Seoul, the events of each Organizer, are collectively referred to as the "Fairs".</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    5. A
			                    <b>
			                        Preview Ticket, General Admission First Preview, General Admission First Access, General Admission Afternoon Access, Student/Youth Ticket, or 2026 Korea Art
			                        Festival Special Discount Ticket
			                    </b>
			                    ("Ticket") will allow entry to both Kiaf SEOUL and Frieze Seoul during the relevant dates and times of the Fairs as determined by the Organizers. All purchasable
			                    tickets are specified below.
			                    <ul class="mt-2 mb-2">
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>Preview Ticket</b> - Multi-day ticket, provides access and re-entry to all General Admission days.</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>General Admission First Preview</b> - Thursday preview access, 1 re-entry on the same day.</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>General Admission First Access</b> - Friday and Saturday access before 3 PM, 1 re-entry on the same day.</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>General Admission Afternoon Access</b> - Friday and Saturday access after 3 PM, 1 re-entry on the same day.</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>Student / Youth Tickets</b> - General Admission Student (7-19 years), valid ID required.</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>2026 Korea Art Festival Special Discount Tickets</b> - Limited quantity discounted tickets for GA First, Afternoon, and Preview Access.</li>
			                    </ul>
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    6. By purchasing any Ticket to the Fairs and/or attending the Fairs using a VIP pass, you ("You") agree to be bound by the terms and conditions set out herein ("Terms
			                    and Conditions") and any other terms drawn to your attention by the Organizers and/or stated on the Ticket.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    7. By purchasing a Student/Youth Ticket (7-19 years) or attending with such a Ticket, You confirm that you can present valid photo ID such as a passport or student ID
			                    to gain entry.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">8. Student/Youth tickets are limited in quantity and may not be available to all individuals aged 7-19.</li>
			                <li class="item">9. One companion may enter for free to assist a ticket holder with disability (for severe disability grades of 2 or higher only).</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    10. These Terms and Conditions and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or
			                    formation, shall be governed by, and construed in accordance with the law of the Republic of Korea.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    11. If any of these Terms and Conditions should be determined to be illegal, invalid or otherwise unenforceable by reason of the law of any state or country in which
			                    these Terms and Conditions are intended to be effective, then to the extent and within the jurisdiction in which that term or condition is illegal, invalid or
			                    unenforceable, it shall be severed and deleted from that term and the remaining Terms and Conditions shall survive and continue to be binding and enforceable.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    12. To the extent permitted in law, any cause of action a Ticket holder may have with respect to their Ticket must be commenced within one (1) year after the claim or
			                    cause of action arises.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">13. Organizers expressly reserve the right to change and/or amend these Terms and Conditions from time to time.</li>
			            </ul>
			
			            <h6>Purchase Conditions & Refund Policy</h6>
			            <ul class="text-black-50 mb-3 small list-unstyled text-indent-1">
			                <li class="item">1. Tickets remain the property of the Organizers and may be recalled.</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    2. Refunds (all times 00:00–23:59) for September 3–5, 2026:
			                    <ul class="mt-2 mb-2">
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>Until 11 days before (August 23, 2026)</b>: Full refund</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>10 days before (August 24, 2026)</b>: 10% deduction</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>7–9 days before (August 25–27, 2026)</b>: 20% deduction</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>3–6 days before (August 28–31, 2026)</b>: 30% deduction</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>1–2 days before (September 1–September 2, 2026)</b>: 90% deduction</li>
			                        <li>&nbsp;<b>On the day of the event (September 3–5, 2026)</b>: No refund</li>
			                    </ul>
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">3. If the Fairs are postponed, tickets remain valid for the rescheduled date. Full refunds available if you cannot attend.</li>
			                <li class="item">4. If the Fairs are cancelled prior to opening, full refund of ticket face value only.</li>
			                <li class="item">5. If a Fair day is curtailed, Organizers may offer partial refunds or reschedule; rescheduled days follow clause 3.</li>
			                <li class="item">6. Travel/accommodation costs are your responsibility; Organizers are not liable.</li>
			                <li class="item">7. Tickets are non-refundable if events are altered due to circumstances beyond Organizers' control.</li>
			                <li class="item">8. By purchasing a Ticket, you confirm you have read and understood these Terms and Conditions.</li>
			            </ul>
			
			            <h6>Entry Conditions</h6>
			            <ul class="text-black-50 mb-0 small list-unstyled text-indent-1">
			                <li class="item">
			                    1. A valid admission Ticket entitles the Ticket holder to attend the Fairs on the date and at the time stated on the Ticket. Visitors will not be allowed admission
			                    without a valid Ticket. Please arrive <b>at least 15 minutes before</b> the time stated. Last admission is <b>30 minutes prior to closing</b>. Latecomers will not be
			                    admitted.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">2. Parking or tour tickets do not grant admission. Admission Ticket(s) must be purchased separately.</li>
			                <li class="item">3. Children aged 7+ need a valid Ticket and photo ID; under 7 enter free with an adult.</li>
			                <li class="item">4. General Admission and Student tickets allow <b>1 re-entry</b> on the same day if scanned out. Preview and VIP tickets allow re-entry.</li>
			                <li class="item">5. No large floral displays may be brought in.</li>
			                <li class="item">6. No unauthorized artwork, performances, or distribution of marketing materials allowed.</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    7. Tickets must not be resold, exchanged, transferred, altered, or defaced. Any such action voids the Ticket. Prohibited practices include photocopies, screenshots,
			                    altered tickets, or illegally produced/distributed tickets.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">8. Security checks may be conducted. Prohibited items may be confiscated; visitors refusing checks may be removed.</li>
			                <li class="item">9. Large bags (backpacks, suitcases, folding bicycles, scooters) are not permitted; limited lockers available.</li>
			                <li class="item">10. Open containers of food, alcohol, sharp items, drones, and laser pens are not allowed.</li>
			                <li class="item">11. Proof of age may be required. Failure to provide ID may result in refusal of alcohol or removal.</li>
			                <li class="item">12. Organizers may refuse entry or evict anyone violating Terms, committing offenses, or behaving dangerously or anti-socially.</li>
			                <li class="item">13. Use of illegal substances is strictly prohibited; only assistance animals are allowed.</li>
			                <li class="item">14. Commercial, promotional, or trading activities require prior written consent.</li>
			                <li class="item">15. All photography/filming rights vest with Organizers. By attending, you consent to being recorded for promotional or security purposes.</li>
			                <li class="item">16. Visitors must follow staff instructions in emergencies.</li>
			                <li class="item">17. Certain exhibits may contain flashing/strobe/neon lights. Exercise caution if photosensitive.</li>
			                <li class="item">
			                    18. Attendance is at your own risk; Organizers are not liable except for death, personal injury caused by negligence, or liabilities that cannot be excluded by law.
			                </li>
			                <li class="item">19. Organizers are not responsible for contracts or advice obtained from any exhibitor.</li>
			            </ul>
			            <a href="https://www.frieze.com/privacy" target="_blank"><u class="text-primary fw-bold">Privacy policy.</u></a>
			        </div>
			    </div>
			</div>
	    </div>
	
												
